# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# The judgment layer (DESIGN.md §7)
#
# Set ONE of the keys below. Without any of them the app still runs: every
# deterministic figure is computed as normal and the agent falls back to the
# plain band rule, labelled as such in the UI.
#
# Check what is loaded:  npm run env:check
# Measure quality:       npm run llm:check -- --n 10
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Google Gemini — free tier, no credit card.
# Key: https://aistudio.google.com/apikey
# The app asks for `gemini-flash-lite-latest`, which is the generous free tier.
# Quotas are per model per day and Google changes them: gemini-2.5-flash was
# measured at 20 requests/day here, which a single backtest exhausts. Check the
# current limits at https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/rate-limits rather
# than trusting a number in this file.
# Budget: 4 model calls per review, 1 per typed instruction.
GEMINI_API_KEY=

# Groq — free tier. Key: https://console.groq.com/keys
# GROQ_API_KEY=

# OpenRouter — some models are free (suffix ":free").
# Key: https://openrouter.ai/keys
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=

# Anthropic — paid. This is what DESIGN.md specifies (claude-sonnet-4-6).
# Key: https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys
# Note: a claude.ai Pro/Max subscription does NOT include API access; the
# Console is a separate account with its own credit.
# ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# --- Overrides -------------------------------------------------------------

# Pick explicitly when several keys are present:
# anthropic | gemini | groq | openrouter | ollama
# LLM_PROVIDER=gemini

# Override the model for the chosen provider.
# LLM_MODEL=gemini-2.5-flash

# Any other OpenAI-compatible endpoint, including a local one.
# Ollama needs no key: LLM_BASE_URL=http://localhost:11434/v1
# LLM_BASE_URL=
# LLM_API_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binance MCP (optional)
#
# Only needed to capture the MCP tool list (npm run mcp:discover) and to place
# orders. Obtain by connecting the server in an MCP client that performs the
# OAuth flow — see README "Connecting the MCP server".
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# BINANCE_MCP_TOKEN=
